WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.090
So Donald Trump continues to tweet and to
say more and more about how he is bringing

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.670
troops home from [inaudible],

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:07.670
from Syria.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:11.810
And this has been one of the big defenses
and justifications for what is actually a

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:16.919
completely shortsighted and haphazard decision
to abandon the Kurds in Northern Syria who

00:00:16.919 --> 00:00:22.270
were immediately attacked by Kurdish forces
after American troops pulled back.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.270
We're bringing troops.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:29.429
Home has been the story, except it turns out
that that is also not true.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.870
Trump tweeted that the troops are coming home
and then the Pentagon chief Mark Esper said,

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.880
well, they're not really coming home.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.969
They're going from Syria to Iraq.

00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:47.190
The troops are actually going to the epicenter
of so called endless war in Iraq.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:53.840
And when you look at the details of the entire
situation, it is truly in every sense, the

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.859
worst of American foreign policy.

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:57.379
And I'll explain what I mean.

00:00:57.379 --> 00:00:59.999
Uh, we abandoned the Kurds in Northern Syria.

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:00.999
Okay.

00:01:00.999 --> 00:01:02.379
So that is a problem.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.060
We immediately have the narrative that getting
troops out of anywhere at any opportunity

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.470
is by default the right thing.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:13.520
And we should be praising Trump for it despite
all of the both circumstantial questions about

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.979
it, foreign policy questions about it, motivational
questions about it, blackmail questions about

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:18.979
it.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:20.610
I mean, all sorts of questions around Trump's
decision.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:27.590
Okay, but we're told we are at least going
to get troops out of harm's way.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:32.340
We're going to get out of an endless commitment
that is all good, even if it has some unintended

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:39.229
consequences like the deaths of Kurds, except
we quietly kept a small number of forces in

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:43.329
Northern Syria anyway, not much publicized.

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:44.690
What are they doing?

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:45.979
Not protecting the curds.

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:49.060
They're protecting oil fields.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:54.070
Oil fields, case in point, prototypical of
American foreign policy.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.640
Abandoned the curds, protect the oil fields.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.190
Okay, but that's not bad enough.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:03.689
Then Mark Esper says in the same statement
where he says, a small number of troops are

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.689
still there protecting oil fields.

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:12.640
He says, all us troops leaving Syria are going
to Western Iraq.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.019
No one is coming home.

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:15.250
The story is false.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:20.860
The United States is not leaving the region,
and it's really important to understand the

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.560
significance of this.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.379
The entire justification for abandoning the
Kurds, opening the door to the resurgence

00:02:28.379 --> 00:02:30.350
of ISIS that we are now dealing with.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:35.980
As the French prime minister recently told
us, it was all about stopping endless and

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.890
indefinite military commitments.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.920
Getting out of the region, taking our troops
out of harm's way.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.659
The troops are moving from Syria to Iraq.

00:02:46.659 --> 00:02:49.800
We aren't ending indefinite military commitments.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.569
We aren't taking those troops out of harm's
way.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:54.200
We're not getting out of the region.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:59.730
We're not doing any of the things that supposedly
are good about the decision to leave Northern

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:08.010
Syria, and we're actually perpetuating many
of the problems that some claim Trump is solving

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.030
by leaving Northern Syria.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:16.140
We're shifting troops around and we're shifting
troops around in a way that has led to Kurds

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.150
being killed.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:23.290
Two, the pleasure, by the way, of Putin and
urge to one, while not accomplishing any of

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.480
the outwardly stated goals.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:30.060
This is a microcosm of foreign policy under
Donald Trump.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.080
It's a combination of everything Trump says
is actually the opposite with not accomplishing

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:42.599
the stated goals, never properly analyzing
what might actually a motivating factor, and

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:48.340
then in the end we're actually doing the opposite
of what it is that we claim to be doing via

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.810
these foreign policy decisions.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:54.050
Now you know the everything Trump says being
the opposite is not new.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.940
There's many examples of that in the Trump
presidency.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.430
Trump says he's going to drain the swamp.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:02.220
He has filled the swamp more than any president
in recent history.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.640
Trump says he knows trade and he's going to
do better on trade than anybody else.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.100
People fall for it.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:13.689
Then he starts a trade war that he can't win
and he absolutely decimates Midwestern farmers

00:04:13.689 --> 00:04:15.230
in the United States.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.210
He says he will end conflicts of interest
with his businesses.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:23.960
He actually has more conflict of interest
than ever.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.610
He's funneling millions of dollars into his
pockets by virtue of being president and those

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.020
pockets of his friends and family, he will
be the most transparent president with the

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.310
most transparent administration.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.750
No press briefings since.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.750
Is it last March?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:42.930
I mean, has it been nearly what, seven, eight,
nine months since the last actual press briefing?

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:46.440
And of course, bring the troops home and get
them out of harm's way and get out of an indefinite

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.840
conflict and an endless conflict.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.550
Uh, and it's the opposite.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.941
It's we'll send them elsewhere while our allies
who have been helping us to fight ISIS, the

00:04:54.941 --> 00:04:57.150
Kurds are getting killed.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:05.300
If you don't see the tragedy that this foreign
policy and this presidency is, then maybe

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.940
you deserve this presidency.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.510
I'm sort of at a loss for how to even sum
it up, but the exact opposite of what we were

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:15.220
told this happening is actually what is happening
on the ground.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.920
And you don't have to go to fake news media
to be told it.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.630
You just read the words of Trump's own Pentagon,
chief Mark Esper.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.540
He's telling you what's going on.

